# Migrating a Flat Pulumi Program to ComponentResources Without Replacement

## The Core Problem

When you wrap existing resources in a `ComponentResource`, Pulumi's URN changes because the URN encodes the parent chain:

```
# Before (flat, parent = stack)
urn:pulumi:prod::acme-platform::aws:s3/bucket:Bucket::assets

# After (parented to component)
urn:pulumi:prod::acme-platform::acme:app:Storage$aws:s3/bucket:Bucket::assets
```

Pulumi sees the old URN disappear and a new URN appear → **delete + create**. For an RDS instance with `deletionProtection: true` that's a failed deployment; for an S3 bucket with objects it's a `BucketNotEmpty` error; for an EKS cluster it's a 20-minute outage.

`aliases` tells the engine "this new URN *is* that old URN" so it adopts the existing state instead.

---

## Part 0 — Getting the Old URNs

Never guess. Export them from the live stack before touching code.

```bash
# Do this for EACH stack, before any refactor
for stack in dev prod; do
  pulumi stack select $stack
  pulumi stack export --file backup-$stack-$(date +%Y%m%d).json
  pulumi stack --show-urns > urns-$stack.txt
done
```

`urns-$stack.txt` is the source of truth for every alias you write.

---

## Part 1 — The "Before" State (flat program)

```
acme-platform/
├── Pulumi.yaml
├── Pulumi.dev.yaml
├── Pulumi.prod.yaml
└── index.ts          # ~400 lines, everything at top level
```

`index.ts` (abridged — the shape that matters):

```typescript
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";
import * as eks from "@pulumi/eks";
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";

const cfg = new pulumi.Config();
const env = pulumi.getStack();                    // "dev" | "prod"
const isProd = env === "prod";

// ---- storage ----
const assets = new aws.s3.BucketV2("assets", { /* ... */ });
new aws.s3.BucketVersioningV2("assets-versioning", { /* ... */ });
new aws.s3.BucketServerSideEncryptionConfigurationV2("assets-sse", { /* ... */ });
new aws.s3.BucketPublicAccessBlock("assets-pab", { /* ... */ });

// ---- database ----
const dbSubnets = new aws.rds.SubnetGroup("db-subnets", { /* ... */ });
const dbSg      = new aws.ec2.SecurityGroup("db-sg", { /* ... */ });
const db        = new aws.rds.Instance("db", { /* ... */ });

// ---- cluster ----
const cluster = new eks.Cluster("app", { /* ... */ });

// ---- identity ----
const svcUser = new aws.iam.User("svc", { /* ... */ });
const svcRole = new aws.iam.Role("svc-role", { /* ... */ });

// ---- edge ----
const cert = new aws.acm.Certificate("cert", { /* ... */ });
const cdn  = new aws.cloudfront.Distribution("cdn", { /* ... */ });
```

---

## Part 2 — The "After" Layout

```
acme-platform/
├── Pulumi.yaml
├── Pulumi.dev.yaml
├── Pulumi.prod.yaml
├── index.ts                    # ~60 lines: wires components together
└── components/
    ├── config.ts               # env → sizing map
    ├── storage.ts              # AssetStorage
    ├── database.ts             # AppDatabase
    ├── cluster.ts              # AppCluster
    ├── identity.ts             # ServiceIdentity
    └── edge.ts                 # HttpsEdge
```

---

## Part 3 — Environment Config (typed, no magic strings)

`components/config.ts`

```typescript
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";

export interface EnvSpec {
    readonly env: "dev" | "prod";
    readonly region: string;
    readonly cluster: { instanceType: string; desiredSize: number; minSize: number; maxSize: number };
    readonly db: { instanceClass: string; multiAz: boolean; storageEncrypted: boolean; backupRetentionDays: number };
    readonly storage: { replicaRegion?: string };
    readonly edge: { useCloudFront: boolean };
}

const SPECS: Record<"dev" | "prod", Omit<EnvSpec, "region">> = {
    dev: {
        env: "dev",
        cluster: { instanceType: "t3.medium", desiredSize: 2, minSize: 2, maxSize: 4 },
        db: { instanceClass: "db.t3.micro", multiAz: false, storageEncrypted: false, backupRetentionDays: 7 },
        storage: {},
        edge: { useCloudFront: false },   // internal ALB
    },
    prod: {
        env: "prod",
        cluster: { instanceType: "t3.large", desiredSize: 4, minSize: 4, maxSize: 8 },
        db: { instanceClass: "db.t3.medium", multiAz: true, storageEncrypted: true, backupRetentionDays: 30 },
        storage: { replicaRegion: "us-west-2" },
        edge: { useCloudFront: true },
    },
};

export function loadEnvSpec(): EnvSpec {
    const stack = pulumi.getStack();
    if (stack !== "dev" && stack !== "prod") {
        throw new Error(`Unknown stack "${stack}"; expected "dev" or "prod"`);
    }
    const region = new pulumi.Config("aws").require("region");
    return { ...SPECS[stack], region };
}
```

`Pulumi.dev.yaml`

```yaml
config:
  aws:region: us-east-1
  acme-platform:dbUsername: appuser
  acme-platform:dbPassword:
    secure: AAABAI9y...        # pulumi config set --secret
  acme-platform:domainName: dev.acme.example
```

`Pulumi.prod.yaml`

```yaml
config:
  aws:region: us-east-1
  acme-platform:dbUsername: appuser
  acme-platform:dbPassword:
    secure: AAABAKm2...
  acme-platform:domainName: app.acme.example
  acme-platform:hostedZoneId: Z0123456789ABCDEFGHIJ
```

---

## Part 4 — The Alias Mechanics

### Two ways to write an alias

**Option A — `aliases: [{ parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }]`** (or `{ parent: undefined }`)

Declarative: "this resource used to have the stack as its parent." Pulumi computes the old URN for you.

**Option B — `aliases: [{ urn: "urn:pulumi:..." }]`**

Explicit full URN. Verbose but unambiguous — use it when the *name* also changed, or when you're not sure the computed form matches.

I use **A on the component itself** and let child aliases be derived, falling back to **B** wherever the resource name changed.

### The key insight: aliases propagate to children

When you put an alias on a `ComponentResource`, Pulumi automatically propagates it down to child resources — a child's old URN is recomputed with the component's aliased URN as parent. **This means for a pure "wrap in component, keep names" refactor, one alias on the component is often enough.**

But there's a catch: the component itself is a *new* resource type in the URN chain. Going from

```
stack → aws:s3/bucket:Bucket::assets
```

to

```
stack → acme:app:Storage::assets-storage → aws:s3/bucket:Bucket::assets
```

means the child's parent went from *stack* to *Storage component*. The alias on the component (`parent: rootStackResource`) makes Pulumi treat `Storage` as if it were previously at root — but `Storage` never existed before, so there's nothing to adopt for it (it's a component, no cloud state, harmless). The **children** still need `aliases: [{ parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }]` because their parent genuinely changed.

**Practical rule I follow: put an explicit alias on every physical resource being reparented.** It costs a line each and removes all ambiguity.

---

## Part 5 — Components With Aliases

### `components/storage.ts`

```typescript
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import { EnvSpec } from "./config";

export interface AssetStorageArgs {
    spec: EnvSpec;
    tags: Record<string, string>;
}

export class AssetStorage extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
    public readonly bucket: aws.s3.BucketV2;
    public readonly bucketArn: pulumi.Output<string>;
    public readonly bucketName: pulumi.Output<string>;

    constructor(name: string, args: AssetStorageArgs, opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions) {
        super("acme:app:AssetStorage", name, {}, opts);

        const { spec, tags } = args;

        // Every child carries an alias saying "I used to hang off the stack root."
        const reparent: pulumi.CustomResourceOptions = {
            parent: this,
            aliases: [{ parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }],
        };

        this.bucket = new aws.s3.BucketV2("assets", {
            forceDestroy: false,
            tags,
        }, reparent);

        new aws.s3.BucketVersioningV2("assets-versioning", {
            bucket: this.bucket.id,
            versioningConfiguration: { status: "Enabled" },
        }, reparent);

        new aws.s3.BucketServerSideEncryptionConfigurationV2("assets-sse", {
            bucket: this.bucket.id,
            rules: [{
                applyServerSideEncryptionByDefault: { sseAlgorithm: "AES256" },
                bucketKeyEnabled: true,
            }],
        }, reparent);

        new aws.s3.BucketPublicAccessBlock("assets-pab", {
            bucket: this.bucket.id,
            blockPublicAcls: true,
            blockPublicPolicy: true,
            ignorePublicAcls: true,
            restrictPublicBuckets: true,
        }, reparent);

        if (spec.storage.replicaRegion) {
            this.setupReplication(spec, tags, reparent);
        }

        this.bucketArn = this.bucket.arn;
        this.bucketName = this.bucket.bucket;

        this.registerOutputs({
            bucketArn: this.bucketArn,
            bucketName: this.bucketName,
        });
    }

    private setupReplication(
        spec: EnvSpec,
        tags: Record<string, string>,
        reparent: pulumi.CustomResourceOptions,
    ) {
        const replicaProvider = new aws.Provider("replica-provider", {
            region: spec.storage.replicaRegion! as aws.Region,
        }, { parent: this, aliases: [{ parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }] });

        const replicaBucket = new aws.s3.BucketV2("assets-replica", { tags }, {
            parent: this,
            provider: replicaProvider,
            aliases: [{ parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }],
        });

        new aws.s3.BucketVersioningV2("assets-replica-versioning", {
            bucket: replicaBucket.id,
            versioningConfiguration: { status: "Enabled" },
        }, { parent: this, provider: replicaProvider, aliases: [{ parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }] });

        new aws.s3.BucketServerSideEncryptionConfigurationV2("assets-replica-sse", {
            bucket: replicaBucket.id,
            rules: [{ applyServerSideEncryptionByDefault: { sseAlgorithm: "AES256" } }],
        }, { parent: this, provider: replicaProvider, aliases: [{ parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }] });

        const replRole = new aws.iam.Role("assets-replication-role", {
            assumeRolePolicy: JSON.stringify({
                Version: "2012-10-17",
                Statement: [{
                    Effect: "Allow",
                    Principal: { Service: "s3.amazonaws.com" },
                    Action: "sts:AssumeRole",
                }],
            }),
            tags,
        }, reparent);

        new aws.iam.RolePolicy("assets-replication-policy", {
            role: replRole.id,
            policy: pulumi.all([this.bucket.arn, replicaBucket.arn]).apply(([src, dst]) =>
                JSON.stringify({
                    Version: "2012-10-17",
                    Statement: [
                        {
                            Effect: "Allow",
                            Action: ["s3:GetReplicationConfiguration", "s3:ListBucket"],
                            Resource: [src],
                        },
                        {
                            Effect: "Allow",
                            Action: [
                                "s3:GetObjectVersionForReplication",
                                "s3:GetObjectVersionAcl",
                                "s3:GetObjectVersionTagging",
                            ],
                            Resource: [`${src}/*`],
                        },
                        {
                            Effect: "Allow",
                            Action: [
                                "s3:ReplicateObject",
                                "s3:ReplicateDelete",
                                "s3:ReplicateTags",
                            ],
                            Resource: [`${dst}/*`],
                        },
                    ],
                }),
            ),
        }, reparent);

        new aws.s3.BucketReplicationConfig("assets-replication", {
            role: replRole.arn,
            bucket: this.bucket.id,
            rules: [{
                id: "replicate-all",
                status: "Enabled",
                filter: {},
                deleteMarkerReplication: { status: "Enabled" },
                destination: {
                    bucket: replicaBucket.arn,
                    storageClass: "STANDARD_IA",
                },
            }],
        }, reparent);
    }
}
```

### `components/database.ts`

```typescript
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import { EnvSpec } from "./config";

export interface AppDatabaseArgs {
    spec: EnvSpec;
    vpcId: pulumi.Input<string>;
    privateSubnetIds: pulumi.Input<pulumi.Input<string>[]>;
    clientSecurityGroupId: pulumi.Input<string>;
    username: pulumi.Input<string>;
    password: pulumi.Output<string>;      // secret
    tags: Record<string, string>;
}

export class AppDatabase extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
    public readonly instance: aws.rds.Instance;
    public readonly connectionString: pulumi.Output<string>;

    constructor(name: string, args: AppDatabaseArgs, opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions) {
        super("acme:app:AppDatabase", name, {}, opts);

        const { spec, tags } = args;
        const reparent: pulumi.CustomResourceOptions = {
            parent: this,
            aliases: [{ parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }],
        };

        const subnetGroup = new aws.rds.SubnetGroup("db-subnets", {
            subnetIds: args.privateSubnetIds,
            tags,
        }, reparent);

        const sg = new aws.ec2.SecurityGroup("db-sg", {
            vpcId: args.vpcId,
            description: "Postgres access from application nodes only",
            ingress: [{
                protocol: "tcp",
                fromPort: 5432,
                toPort: 5432,
                securityGroups: [args.clientSecurityGroupId],
            }],
            egress: [],
            tags,
        }, reparent);

        this.instance = new aws.rds.Instance("db", {
            engine: "postgres",
            engineVersion: "16.3",
            instanceClass: spec.db.instanceClass,
            allocatedStorage: spec.env === "prod" ? 100 : 20,
            maxAllocatedStorage: spec.env === "prod" ? 500 : 50,
            dbName: "appdb",
            username: args.username,
            password: args.password,
            dbSubnetGroupName: subnetGroup.name,
            vpcSecurityGroupIds: [sg.id],

            // --- acceptance criteria ---
            publiclyAccessible: false,
            deletionProtection: true,
            backupRetentionPeriod: spec.db.backupRetentionDays,   // >= 7
            storageEncrypted: spec.db.storageEncrypted,
            multiAz: spec.db.multiAz,

            storageType: "gp3",
            backupWindow: "03:00-04:00",
            maintenanceWindow: "sun:04:30-sun:05:30",
            skipFinalSnapshot: false,
            finalSnapshotIdentifier: `${spec.env}-appdb-final`,
            applyImmediately: false,
            autoMinorVersionUpgrade: true,
            performanceInsightsEnabled: spec.env === "prod",
            enabledCloudwatchLogsExports: ["postgresql", "upgrade"],
            tags,
        }, {
            ...reparent,
            // Extra safety net during the migration window.
            protect: true,
            ignoreChanges: ["password"],
        });

        this.connectionString = pulumi.secret(
            pulumi.interpolate`postgresql://${args.username}:${args.password}@${this.instance.address}:${this.instance.port}/appdb`,
        );

        this.registerOutputs({ endpoint: this.instance.address });
    }
}
```

### `components/cluster.ts`

```typescript
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";
import * as eks from "@pulumi/eks";
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import { EnvSpec } from "./config";

export interface AppClusterArgs {
    spec: EnvSpec;
    vpcId: pulumi.Input<string>;
    publicSubnetIds: pulumi.Input<string[]>;
    privateSubnetIds: pulumi.Input<string[]>;
    tags: Record<string, string>;
}

export class AppCluster extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
    public readonly cluster: eks.Cluster;
    public readonly kubeconfig: pulumi.Output<string>;
    public readonly oidcProviderArn: pulumi.Output<string>;
    public readonly oidcProviderUrl: pulumi.Output<string>;
    public readonly nodeSecurityGroupId: pulumi.Output<string>;

    constructor(name: string, args: AppClusterArgs, opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions) {
        super("acme:app:AppCluster", name, {}, opts);

        const { spec, tags } = args;

        this.cluster = new eks.Cluster("app", {
            vpcId: args.vpcId,
            publicSubnetIds: args.publicSubnetIds,
            privateSubnetIds: args.privateSubnetIds,
            version: "1.30",
            createOidcProvider: true,
            skipDefaultNodeGroup: true,
            endpointPublicAccess: spec.env !== "prod",
            endpointPrivateAccess: true,
            nodeAssociatePublicIpAddress: false,
            tags,
        }, {
            parent: this,
            aliases: [{ parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }],
        });

        // eks.Cluster is itself a ComponentResource; its own children are
        // aliased automatically because their parent (the cluster) is aliased.

        const ngRole = new aws.iam.Role("app-ng-role", {
            assumeRolePolicy: aws.iam.assumeRolePolicyForPrincipal({ Service: "ec2.amazonaws.com" }),
            tags,
        }, { parent: this, aliases: [{ parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }] });

        for (const [i, policyArn] of [
            aws.iam.ManagedPolicy.AmazonEKSWorkerNodePolicy,
            aws.iam.ManagedPolicy.AmazonEKS_CNI_Policy,
            aws.iam.ManagedPolicy.AmazonEC2ContainerRegistryReadOnly,
        ].entries()) {
            new aws.iam.RolePolicyAttachment(`app-ng-attach-${i}`, {
                role: ngRole.name,
                policyArn,
            }, { parent: this, aliases: [{ parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }] });
        }

        new eks.ManagedNodeGroup("app-nodes", {
            cluster: this.cluster,
            nodeRole: ngRole,
            subnetIds: args.privateSubnetIds,
            instanceTypes: [spec.cluster.instanceType],
            scalingConfig: {
                desiredSize: spec.cluster.desiredSize,
                minSize: spec.cluster.minSize,
                maxSize: spec.cluster.maxSize,
            },
            labels: { env: spec.env },
            tags,
        }, { parent: this, aliases: [{ parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }] });

        this.kubeconfig = pulumi.secret(this.cluster.kubeconfig.apply(JSON.stringify));
        this.oidcProviderArn = this.cluster.core.oidcProvider!.arn;
        this.oidcProviderUrl = this.cluster.core.oidcProvider!.url;
        this.nodeSecurityGroupId = this.cluster.nodeSecurityGroup.id;

        this.registerOutputs({});
    }
}
```

### `components/identity.ts`

```typescript
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import { EnvSpec } from "./config";

export interface ServiceIdentityArgs {
    spec: EnvSpec;
    bucketArn: pulumi.Input<string>;
    oidcProviderArn: pulumi.Input<string>;
    oidcProviderUrl: pulumi.Input<string>;
    serviceAccountNamespace: string;
    serviceAccountName: string;
    tags: Record<string, string>;
}

export class ServiceIdentity extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
    public readonly roleArn: pulumi.Output<string>;
    public readonly accessKeyId?: pulumi.Output<string>;
    public readonly secretAccessKey?: pulumi.Output<string>;

    constructor(name: string, args: ServiceIdentityArgs, opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions) {
        super("acme:app:ServiceIdentity", name, {}, opts);

        const { spec, tags } = args;
        const reparent: pulumi.CustomResourceOptions = {
            parent: this,
            aliases: [{ parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }],
        };

        // Least-privilege document — explicit actions, scoped ARNs, no wildcards.
        const accessPolicy = pulumi.output(args.bucketArn).apply(arn =>
            JSON.stringify({
                Version: "2012-10-17",
                Statement: [
                    {
                        Sid: "ListAssetBucket",
                        Effect: "Allow",
                        Action: ["s3:ListBucket", "s3:GetBucketLocation"],
                        Resource: arn,
                    },
                    {
                        Sid: "ReadWriteAssets",
                        Effect: "Allow",
                        Action: ["s3:GetObject", "s3:PutObject", "s3:DeleteObject"],
                        Resource: `${arn}/*`,
                    },
                ],
            }),
        );

        const policy = new aws.iam.Policy("svc-policy", {
            description: `Least-privilege asset access (${spec.env})`,
            policy: accessPolicy,
            tags,
        }, reparent);

        // OIDC-trusted role (IRSA) — used by workloads in both envs.
        const trust = pulumi
            .all([args.oidcProviderArn, args.oidcProviderUrl])
            .apply(([providerArn, providerUrl]) => {
                const host = providerUrl.replace("https://", "");
                return JSON.stringify({
                    Version: "2012-10-17",
                    Statement: [{
                        Effect: "Allow",
                        Principal: { Federated: providerArn },
                        Action: "sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity",
                        Condition: {
                            StringEquals: {
                                [`${host}:aud`]: "sts.amazonaws.com",
                                [`${host}:sub`]:
                                    `system:serviceaccount:${args.serviceAccountNamespace}:${args.serviceAccountName}`,
                            },
                        },
                    }],
                });
            });

        const role = new aws.iam.Role("svc-role", {
            assumeRolePolicy: trust,
            maxSessionDuration: 3600,
            tags,
        }, reparent);

        new aws.iam.RolePolicyAttachment("svc-role-policy", {
            role: role.name,
            policyArn: policy.arn,
        }, reparent);

        this.roleArn = role.arn;

        // Programmatic IAM user: dev only. Prod is OIDC-only.
        if (spec.env === "dev") {
            const user = new aws.iam.User("svc", {
                path: "/service/",
                forceDestroy: true,
                tags,
            }, reparent);

            new aws.iam.UserPolicyAttachment("svc-user-policy", {
                user: user.name,
                policyArn: policy.arn,
            }, reparent);

            const key = new aws.iam.AccessKey("svc-key", { user: user.name }, reparent);
            this.accessKeyId = key.id;
            this.secretAccessKey = pulumi.secret(key.secret);
        }

        this.registerOutputs({ roleArn: this.roleArn });
    }
}
```

### `components/edge.ts`

```typescript
import * as aws from "@pulumi/aws";
import * as pulumi from "@pulumi/pulumi";
import { EnvSpec } from "./config";

export interface HttpsEdgeArgs {
    spec: EnvSpec;
    domainName: string;
    hostedZoneId?: string;
    vpcId: pulumi.Input<string>;
    subnetIds: pulumi.Input<string[]>;
    tags: Record<string, string>;
}

export class HttpsEdge extends pulumi.ComponentResource {
    public readonly url: pulumi.Output<string>;

    constructor(name: string, args: HttpsEdgeArgs, opts?: pulumi.ComponentResourceOptions) {
        super("acme:app:HttpsEdge", name, {}, opts);

        const { spec, tags } = args;
        const reparent: pulumi.CustomResourceOptions = {
            parent: this,
            aliases: [{ parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }],
        };

        const albSg = new aws.ec2.SecurityGroup("alb-sg", {
            vpcId: args.vpcId,
            ingress: [{ protocol: "tcp", fromPort: 443, toPort: 443, cidrBlocks: ["0.0.0.0/0"] }],
            egress: [{ protocol: "-1", fromPort: 0, toPort: 0, cidrBlocks: ["0.0.0.0/0"] }],
            tags,
        }, reparent);

        const alb = new aws.lb.LoadBalancer("app-alb", {
            loadBalancerType: "application",
            internal: !spec.edge.useCloudFront,   // dev: internal ALB
            securityGroups: [albSg.id],
            subnets: args.subnetIds,
            enableHttp2: true,
            idleTimeout: 60,
            tags,
        }, reparent);

        const tg = new aws.lb.TargetGroup("app-tg", {
            port: 8080,
            protocol: "HTTP",
            targetType: "ip",
            vpcId: args.vpcId,
            healthCheck: { path: "/healthz", matcher: "200", interval: 15, timeout: 5 },
            tags,
        }, reparent);

        // Regional cert for the ALB listener.
        const albCert = new aws.acm.Certificate("cert", {
            domainName: args.domainName,
            validationMethod: "DNS",
            tags,
        }, reparent);

        let albCertArn: pulumi.Output<string> = albCert.arn;

        if (args.hostedZoneId) {
            const validationRecord = new aws.route53.Record("cert-validation", {
                zoneId: args.hostedZoneId,
                name: albCert.domainValidationOptions[0].resourceRecordName,
                type: albCert.domainValidationOptions[0].resourceRecordType,
                records: [albCert.domainValidationOptions[0].resourceRecordValue],
                ttl: 60,
                allowOverwrite: true,
            }, reparent);

            const validated = new aws.acm.CertificateValidation("cert-validation-wait", {
                certificateArn: albCert.arn,
                validationRecordFqdns: [validationRecord.fqdn],
            }, reparent);

            albCertArn = validated.certificateArn;
        }

        // HTTPS listener on 443. No forced 80 -> 443 redirect (per spec).
        new aws.lb.Listener("app-https", {
            loadBalancerArn: alb.arn,
            port: 443,
            protocol: "HTTPS",
            sslPolicy: "ELBSecurityPolicy-TLS13-1-2-2021-06",
            certificateArn: albCertArn,
            defaultActions: [{ type: "forward", targetGroupArn: tg.arn }],
        }, reparent);

        if (!spec.edge.useCloudFront) {
            this.url = pulumi.interpolate`https://${alb.dnsName}`;
            this.registerOutputs({ url: this.url });
            return;
        }

        // ---- prod: CloudFront + ACM cert in us-east-1 ----
        const usEast1 = new aws.Provider("us-east-1-provider", { region: "us-east-1" }, {
            parent: this,
            aliases: [{ parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }],
        });

        const cdnCert = new aws.acm.Certificate("cdn-cert", {
            domainName: args.domainName,
            validationMethod: "DNS",
            tags,
        }, { parent: this, provider: usEast1, aliases: [{ parent: pulumi.rootStackResource }] });

        const cdn = new aws.cloudfront.Distribution("cdn", {
            enabled: true,
            aliases: [args.domainName],
