## Part 9 — Rollout Order

```bash
# 1. Snapshot everything
pulumi stack select dev  && pulumi stack export --file backup-dev.json
pulumi stack select prod && pulumi stack export --file backup-prod.json

# 2. Refresh so state matches reality (avoids confusing drift with migration diffs)
pulumi refresh --stack dev --yes
pulumi refresh --stack prod --yes

# 3. Dev first
./scripts/verify-migration.sh dev
pulumi up --stack dev --yes

# 4. Confirm dev is genuinely healthy, not just "preview was clean"
pulumi stack --stack dev --show-urns | grep -c "acme:app:"   # expect 5
curl -sfo /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' "https://$(pulumi stack output appUrl --stack dev | sed 's|https://||')/healthz"

# 5. Prod, gated on a human
./scripts/verify-migration.sh prod
pulumi up --stack prod        # interactive, read the diff again

# 6. Once both stacks are migrated and stable (a week or two),
#    optionally strip aliases in a follow-up PR — preview must stay clean.
```

Environment isolation holds throughout: `dev` and `prod` are separate stacks with separate state files, and every step above is per-stack. Migrating `dev` cannot touch `prod` state.

